<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Viminacium</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Viminacium was a Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">legionary</a> fortress and city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> near modern Kostolac in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, the capital of the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moesia">Moesia</a> Superior. Home of the Seventh Claudian Legion, it grew into one of the largest cities of the Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>, with an amphitheatre and baths. It was sacked by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a> in the 440s and rebuilt under Justinian; excavations have uncovered many buildings and thousands of graves.</p></div>
